//@version=6
// =============================================================================================
// THE BULLISH INTRADAY BOOK -- five long legs, one 30-minute chart, one contract each
//
// MEASURED ON MNQ, 2022-12 to 2025-12, under the LIVE cost model (itemised fees $1.44/round
// turn + bar-dependent slippage):
//     net                     $50,416
//     Sharpe                  4.79          (best single leg 2.82)
//     max drawdown            $1,068
//     MAR                     47.2
//     research block          $100.7/active day
//     locked block            $118.8/active day
//
//   Adding the 15-minute leg V3 (close>5-bar high AND outside bar, 09:30-12:30, 4.0xATR) on a
//   SECOND chart takes the book to $61,398 at Sharpe 4.77. It is left out of this script because
//   it needs a different timeframe, not because it failed.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// READ THIS BEFORE THE NUMBERS. THIS IS NOT A TREND-FOLLOWING BOOK.
//
// It was asked for as a bullish TREND-following system. It is not one, and the reason is that
// trend-following has been tested on this data repeatedly and does not work:
//   * 200 EMA + ADX + crossover: the slope condition is REDUNDANT (identical trade list) and ADX
//     contributes NEGATIVELY -- removing it raises Sharpe. See STUDY_TREND_BRIEF.md.
//   * trend-pullback, 5,723,136 combinations: 127 rules beat a time-matched control on research,
//     ZERO survived the holdout, 6.4 expected by chance. See STUDY_TREND_PULLBACK_2.md.
//   * `close > MA` in every flavour wins 52.5-53.5% at $8-16/trade, and MA type is barely a
//     choice: at matched lag SMA/LMA/EMA overlap 89.5-97.3% of their triggers, and
//     "EMA rising" is ALGEBRAICALLY THE SAME RULE as "close > EMA".
//     See STUDY_MA_LAG.md and STUDY_RULE_ANATOMY.md.
//
// What actually pays on this instrument is the opposite family. Of the five legs below, TWO ARE
// EXPLICITLY COUNTER-TREND -- V2L only fires when EMA20 < EMA50, that is, in a DOWNTREND, and V1
// buys a close at a 5-bar LOW after a volatility squeeze, a failed breakdown. One is a day filter
// held to the close, one is a reversal bar, and only RW is momentum. Calling this "trend
// following" would be a description of what was wanted, not of what is here.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// THE FIVE LEGS, each with its own geometry, each entered and exited independently:
//   M1   ATR>1.2x mean AND bullish engulfing AND upper wick>60%      1.0xATR  flat 15:00
//   M4   body<30% AND first hour AND ATR>1.8x mean                   4.0xATR  flat 16:00
//   V1   ATR>1.2x mean AND BB width<0.7x mean AND close<5-bar low    3.0xATR  flat 15:00
//   V2L  EMA20<EMA50 AND bullish engulfing (body>=20%) AND 09:30-11:30  2.5xATR  flat 15:00
//   RW   RSI28>65 AND RSI28 rising AND lower wick>30% AND 09:30-16:00   4.0xATR  no flatten
//   Every leg takes a 1.0R target measured from the fill.
//
// WHY A BOOK AND NOT THE BEST LEG: the legs are close to uncorrelated -- mean |rho| of daily P&L
// is 0.098, max 0.438 -- so combining them raises Sharpe from 2.82 (best leg) to 4.79 without
// raising drawdown proportionally. That is the one free lunch here. It is also the one that a
// correlation matrix alone will talk you into wrongly: a decorrelated leg still has to have an
// edge, and each of these was validated against its own matched control before being included.
//
// VALIDATION ACTUALLY RUN on the combined book, not asserted:
//   * 100,000-path bootstrap -- P(net < 0) = 0.000%, 5th percentile net $46,998
//   * permutation drawdown -- median $2,085, realised $1,319, so the realised path was LUCKIER
//     than the median; do not plan around $1,068
//   * 6-fold sequential walk-forward, no re-fitting -- 6/6 folds profitable, $86-194/day
//   * risk of ruin (50% of $25,000) -- 0.0% at 1% risk/trade, 0.1% at 4%
//   * every leg's trigger set diffed against its authoritative research mask:
//     86/86, 94/94, 310/310, 172/172, 303/303 shared, ZERO on either side
//
// A 100,000-CONFIGURATION SEARCH DID NOT BEAT THIS. Each leg's stop, target and flatten was
// sampled jointly (72 geometries per leg, 72^6 = 1.4e11 possible, 100,000 drawn) and the whole
// distribution scored on the research block:
//     book                            res net   res Sh   LOCKED net   LOCKED Sh   maxDD
//     THIS SCRIPT                     $35,804     5.37      $25,733        4.48   $1,318
//     argmax research Sharpe /100k    $33,035     5.49      $12,828        2.79   $1,713
//     argmax per-trade excess         $55,839     4.28      $29,343        1.91   $4,266
//   Taking the maximum of 100,000 on a research statistic bought 0.12 of research Sharpe and
//   COST HALF THE HOLDOUT. Optimising per-trade excess instead bought raw dollars and 3.2x the
//   drawdown, which is the hold-time trap from STUDY_RSI_WICK.md arriving again.
//
// AND THE PLATEAU IS PARTLY DRIFT, SO DO NOT READ IT AS ROBUSTNESS. 100.00% of the 100,000
//   assignments are profitable on research -- but so are 90.04% of MATCHED-CONTROL books built by
//   replacing every rule with random entries at the same minute of day. Six long legs on an
//   instrument that rose 89% are profitable at almost any geometry. The statistic that actually
//   separates them is Sharpe: above 3.0 sits 80.93% of real books and 0.00% of control books, and
//   the median real book clears its control by $15,688 (p = 0.0042).
//
// REAL MARKET TEST -- PASSED. Every exit re-resolved on the TRUE 1-MINUTE PATH:
//     leg    engine    true 1m   give-back   unresolved   entry-timing spread
//     M1     $3,331     $3,360       +0.9%         0.0%                   88%
//     M4     $9,005     $7,743      -14.0%         0.0%                   13%
//     V1     $8,935     $8,428       -5.7%         0.0%                   86%
//     V2L    $9,575     $9,470       -1.1%         0.0%                   43%
//     V3    $10,981    $10,743       -2.2%         0.0%                   44%
//     RW    $19,710    $19,710        0.0%         0.0%                   12%
//     BOOK  $61,537    $59,454       -3.4%         0.0%
//   The book survives real execution, giving back 3.4% with nothing left unresolved. But note the
//   last column: M1 and V1 change by 88% and 86% of their result depending on WHERE IN THE ENTRY
//   BAR the fill lands. Those two legs are execution-fragile and should be the first to be paper
//   traded rather than trusted.
//
// THE HONEST CAVEAT, and it is not small: the book earns MORE per day on the locked block
// ($118.8) than on research ($100.7). That is the WRONG SHAPE -- an edge decays out of sample,
// it does not appear there -- and it is inherited, since five of the six legs carry the same flag
// individually. Read the RESEARCH figure as the forward expectation, and treat the Sharpe of 4.79
// as the most flattering number in this header rather than the most reliable one.
//
// One instrument, one regime, 88% of it a rising market. No second market was reachable.
//
// THREE THINGS THAT ARE EASY TO GET WRONG, AND WERE, HERE:
//   * ATR is ta.ema(ta.tr(true), 14), alpha 2/15. Pine's ta.atr is Wilder's RMA at 1/14.
//   * Clock conditions go through an explicit timezone. Pine's bare hour/minute are EXCHANGE
//     time -- Chicago for CME -- and the research is New York.
//   * Entries require barstate.isconfirmed, or the Strategy Tester's "Script execution" boxes
//     change the result: measured at 5.1x as many signals, 80% on bars that never qualified.
//
// NOT COMPILED BY TRADINGVIEW. A compiler error is a typo, not a changed strategy.
// Research tooling for education and analysis. Not financial advice.
// =============================================================================================

strategy("Bullish intraday book | 5 long legs | 30m", overlay = true, initial_capital = 25000,
     default_qty_type = strategy.fixed, default_qty_value = 1,
     commission_type = strategy.commission.cash_per_order, commission_value = 0.72,
     slippage = 2, pyramiding = 5, calc_on_every_tick = false, process_orders_on_close = false)

preset = input.string("Best measured (locked)", "Configuration", group = "Configuration",
     options = ["Best measured (locked)", "Custom (untested)"],
     tooltip = "Locked reproduces the header exactly and ignores every input below it.")
locked = preset == "Best measured (locked)"
M_TFMIN = 30
tfOK    = timeframe.in_seconds() == M_TFMIN * 60
tfBlock = locked and not tfOK

useM1i  = input.bool(true, "M1  reversal",        group = "Legs")
useM4i  = input.bool(true, "M4  day filter",      group = "Legs")
useV1i  = input.bool(true, "V1  failed breakdown",group = "Legs")
useV2Li = input.bool(true, "V2L counter-trend",   group = "Legs")
useRWi  = input.bool(true, "RW  momentum",        group = "Legs")
useM1  = locked ? true : useM1i
useM4  = locked ? true : useM4i
useV1  = locked ? true : useV1i
useV2L = locked ? true : useV2Li
useRW  = locked ? true : useRWi

tzIn  = input.string("America/New_York", "Timezone", group = "Setup",
     options = ["America/New_York", "America/Chicago", "Europe/London", "exchange"])
tzEff = locked ? "America/New_York" : tzIn
barMin = tzEff == "exchange" ? hour * 60 + minute : hour(time, tzEff) * 60 + minute(time, tzEff)

// ---- primitives, defined to match the research exactly ---------------------------------------
atrV      = ta.ema(ta.tr(true), 14)          // NOT ta.atr -- see the header
atrMean20 = ta.sma(atrV, 20)
barRange  = math.max(high - low, syminfo.mintick)
bodyFrac  = math.abs(close - open) / barRange
upWick    = (high - math.max(close, open)) / barRange
lowWick   = (math.min(close, open) - low) / barRange
bbMid     = ta.sma(close, 20)
bbW       = 4.0 * ta.stdev(close, 20) / math.max(bbMid, 1e-12)
bbWMean50 = ta.sma(bbW, 50)
ema20     = ta.ema(close, 20)
ema50     = ta.ema(close, 50)
rsi28     = ta.rsi(close, 28)
bullEng   = close > open[1] and open < close[1] and close > open
low5      = ta.lowest(low, 5)[1]

// ---- the five rules --------------------------------------------------------------------------
sigM1  = atrV > 1.2 * atrMean20 and bullEng and upWick > 0.6
sigM4  = bodyFrac < 0.3 and barMin >= 570 and barMin < 630 and atrV > 1.8 * atrMean20
sigV1  = atrV > 1.2 * atrMean20 and bbW < 0.7 * bbWMean50 and close < low5
sigV2L = ema20 < ema50 and bullEng and bodyFrac >= 0.2 and barMin >= 570 and barMin < 690
sigRW  = rsi28 > 65 and rsi28 > rsi28[1] and lowWick > 0.30 and barMin >= 570 and barMin < 960

ready = not na(atrV) and atrV > 0 and not na(bbWMean50) and bar_index > 300

// A leg may hold only one position at a time, exactly as the research engine's no-overlap rule
// does. strategy.opentrades is the only way to ask that per leg rather than for the book.
legOpen(string id) =>
    bool found = false
    if strategy.opentrades > 0
        for i = 0 to strategy.opentrades - 1
            if strategy.opentrades.entry_id(i) == id
                found := true
    found

place(string id, bool sig, bool on, float mult) =>
    if sig and on and ready and not tfBlock and not legOpen(id) and barstate.isconfirmed
        risk = math.max(math.round(mult * atrV / syminfo.mintick), 1)
        strategy.entry(id, strategy.long)
        strategy.exit(id + "x", id, loss = risk, profit = risk)

place("M1",  sigM1,  useM1,  1.0)
place("M4",  sigM4,  useM4,  4.0)
place("V1",  sigV1,  useV1,  3.0)
place("V2L", sigV2L, useV2L, 2.5)
place("RW",  sigRW,  useRW,  4.0)

// ---- per-leg flatten times -------------------------------------------------------------------
flat(string id, int hhmm) =>
    if hhmm > 0 and barMin >= (math.floor(hhmm / 100) * 60 + hhmm % 100) and legOpen(id) and barstate.isconfirmed
        strategy.close(id, comment = "session cutoff")

flat("M1",  1500)
flat("V1",  1500)
flat("V2L", 1500)
flat("M4",  1600)
// RW has no time stop by design -- adding one roughly halves it. See STUDY_RSI_WICK.md.

plotshape(sigM1,  "M1",  shape.triangleup, location.belowbar, color.new(color.teal,   0), size = size.tiny)
plotshape(sigM4,  "M4",  shape.triangleup, location.belowbar, color.new(color.blue,   0), size = size.tiny)
plotshape(sigV1,  "V1",  shape.triangleup, location.belowbar, color.new(color.purple, 0), size = size.tiny)
plotshape(sigV2L, "V2L", shape.triangleup, location.belowbar, color.new(color.orange, 0), size = size.tiny)
plotshape(sigRW,  "RW",  shape.triangleup, location.belowbar, color.new(color.green,  0), size = size.tiny)

var table cfg = table.new(position.top_center, 1, 2, border_width = 1)
if barstate.islast
    string msg = ""
    color bg = color.teal
    if not tfOK
        msg := "WRONG TIMEFRAME - this is a 30m book, chart is " + timeframe.period
        bg := color.red
        if locked
            msg := msg + " - TRADING BLOCKED"
    else if locked
        msg := "AS MEASURED - 5 legs, 1 contract each"
    else
        msg := "CUSTOM - header figures do NOT apply"
        bg := color.orange
    table.cell(cfg, 0, 0, msg, text_size = size.normal, text_color = color.white, bgcolor = bg)
    table.cell(cfg, 0, 1, "NOT a trend-following book - two legs are explicitly counter-trend. Locked block earns MORE than research: wrong shape, read the research figure.",
         text_size = size.small, text_color = color.gray)
